{"id":"the-recipe-for-anticlockwise-siteswaps","name":"The recipe for anticlockwise siteswaps","chapter":"Six handed siteswaps","kind":"guide","page":113,"label":"112","jugglers":null,"objects":null,"timing":null,"pdf":"https://www.jugglingedge.com/pdf/highgate.pdf#page=113&view=FitH,742","passist":null,"passist_candidate":null,"p4ssist":null,"notations":[{"type":"hg-siteswap-in-text","value":"b9aab939abb6a69"},{"type":"hg-siteswap-in-text","value":"534453"},{"type":"hg-siteswap-in-text","value":"334550403"},{"type":"hg-siteswap-in-text","value":"b9aab939abb6a69"}],"derived":{"kind":"local-6hss","global":"b9aab939abb6a69","confidence":"low","matches_stated":null,"per_juggler":{"A":"a9a69","B":"ba3ba","C":"9b9b6"}},"body":[{"t":"li","h":"Take any siteswap. I&#x27;m going to choose the nine object pattern b9aab939abb6a69. (In"},{"t":"p","h":"siteswap &#x27;a&#x27; stands for 10 and &#x27;b&#x27; stands for 11)."},{"t":"li","h":"Subtract 6 from every number to give a derived siteswap. In my example the derived"},{"t":"p","h":"siteswap is 534453-334550403. (Despite the negative numbers, this is still a siteswap)!"},{"t":"li","h":"Number the beats in a causal diagram as follows:"},{"t":"d","i":0},{"t":"p","h":"Note that the beats are numbered anticlockwise around the triangle of jugglers."},{"t":"li","h":"Now for the first beat, 1, add the first number in the derived siteswap, 5, and you get 1+5=6."},{"t":"p","h":"So on the diagram draw a line from beat 1 to beat 6:"},{"t":"li","h":"Note that 5 is the derived siteswap on beats 5, 10, and 11. So we can draw a similar line"},{"t":"p","h":"starting at each of these beats. Also the pattern repeats, so we can draw a similar line from beats 16, 20, 25, and 26:"},{"t":"d","i":1},{"t":"li","h":"For the second beat, 2, add the second number in the derived siteswap, 3, and you get"},{"t":"p","h":"2+3=5. So on the diagram draw a line from beat 2 to beat 5:"},{"t":"d","i":2},{"t":"li","h":"Note that 3 is the derived siteswap on beats 6, 8, and 15. So we can draw a similar line"},{"t":"p","h":"starting at each of these beats. Also the pattern repeats, so we can draw a similar line from beats 17, 21, 23, and 30:"},{"t":"d","i":3},{"t":"li","h":"For the third beat, 3, add the third number in the derived siteswap, 4, and you get 3+4=7."},{"t":"p","h":"So on the diagram draw a line from beat 3 to beat 7:"},{"t":"d","i":4},{"t":"li","h":"Note that 4 is the derived siteswap on beats 4, 9, and 13. So we can draw a similar line"},{"t":"p","h":"starting at each of these beats. Also the pattern repeats, so we can draw a similar line from beats 18, 19, 24, and 28:"},{"t":"d","i":5},{"t":"li","h":"For the seventh beat, 7, add the seventh number in the derived siteswap, -3, and you get"},{"t":"p","h":"7-3=4. So on the diagram draw a line from beat 7 to beat 4:"},{"t":"d","i":6},{"t":"li","h":"Also the pattern repeats, so we can draw a similar line from beat 22:"},{"t":"d","i":7},{"t":"li","h":"For the twelfth beat, 12, add the twelfth number in the derived siteswap, 0, and you get"},{"t":"p","h":"12+0=12. So on the diagram draw a line from beat 12 to beat 12 (or leave it out)."},{"t":"li","h":"Note that 0 is the derived siteswap on beat 14. So we could draw a similar line starting at"},{"t":"p","h":"that beat. Also the pattern repeats, so we could draw a similar line from beats 27, and 29."},{"t":"li","h":"The result is the following pattern:"},{"t":"d","i":8},{"t":"p","h":"Ben feeds on Martin&#x27;s one count. His pattern is Anne Clare zip Anne Clare. Ben throws straight passes to Anne and crossing passes to Clare. Clare and Anne pass to Ben on Jim&#x27;s two count. Clare starts left handed, a third of a beat after Ben. Her pattern is self pass self pass hold with straight passes to Ben. Anne starts two thirds of a beat after Ben. Her pattern is pass self pass hold self with crossing passes to Ben."},{"t":"p","h":"If we relabel the beats in Clare&#x27;s pattern then all Ben&#x27;s passes are straight and Anne and Clare throw crossing passes to Ben:"},{"t":"d","i":9},{"t":"p","h":"This pattern is Martin&#x27;s one count feeding Jim&#x27;s two count. The anticlockwise siteswap for this feed is: b9aab939abb6a69."}],"drawings":[{"file":"p113-1.png","kind":"causal diagram","reading":{"rows":[{"juggler":"A","name":"Anne","offset":0.6666666666666666,"tempo":1.0,"beats":[{"t":0.6666666666666666,"hand":"R","n":3},{"t":1.6666666666666667,"hand":"L","n":6},{"t":2.6666666666666665,"hand":"R","n":9},{"t":3.6666666666666665,"hand":"L","n":12},{"t":4.666666666666667,"hand":"R","n":15},{"t":5.666666666666667,"hand":"L","n":18},{"t":6.666666666666667,"hand":"R","n":21},{"t":7.666666666666667,"hand":"L","n":24},{"t":8.666666666666666,"hand":"R","n":27},{"t":9.666666666666666,"hand":"L","n":30},{"t":10.666666666666666,"hand":"R"}]},{"juggler":"B","name":"Ben","offset":0.0,"tempo":1.0,"beats":[{"t":0.0,"hand":"R","n":1},{"t":1.0,"hand":"L","n":4},{"t":2.0,"hand":"R","n":7},{"t":3.0,"hand":"L","n":10},{"t":4.0,"hand":"R","n":13},{"t":5.0,"hand":"L","n":16},{"t":6.0,"hand":"R","n":19},{"t":7.0,"hand":"L","n":22},{"t":8.0,"hand":"R","n":25},{"t":9.0,"hand":"L","n":28},{"t":10.0,"hand":"R"}]},{"juggler":"C","name":"Clare","offset":0.3333333333333333,"tempo":1.0,"beats":[{"t":0.3333333333333333,"hand":"L","n":2},{"t":1.3333333333333333,"hand":"R","n":5},{"t":2.3333333333333335,"hand":"L","n":8},{"t":3.3333333333333335,"hand":"R","n":11},{"t":4.333333333333333,"hand":"L","n":14},{"t":5.333333333333333,"hand":"R","n":17},{"t":6.333333333333333,"hand":"L","n":20},{"t":7.333333333333333,"hand":"R","n":23},{"t":8.333333333333334,"hand":"L","n":26},{"t":9.333333333333334,"hand":"R","n":29},{"t":10.333333333333334,"hand":"L"}]}],"arrows":[],"holds":"unlinked","sync":false,"grid":3,"unit_px":63.0,"layout":{"x0":127.0,"unit":63.0,"rows_y":[52.0,115.0,178.0],"names":[[11,34,100,63,"Anne"],[11,160,100,189,"Clare"],[36,97,100,126,"Ben"]],"dots":[[117.5,52.9],[19.1,113.5],[117.5,178.5]]},"tempos":[1.0],"